# Caddy reverse-proxy template for the OPTIONAL public-HTTPS dashboard path (ELO-24).
# Rendered by deploy/bootstrap.sh (step 8) only when DASHBOARD_DOMAIN is set:
#   {{DOMAIN}} -> your dashboard hostname, {{EMAIL}} -> Let's Encrypt account email.
#
# Caddy terminates TLS (auto-provisioned + auto-renewed) and proxies to the
# loopback-bound Next.js dashboard. The operator HTTP Basic-Auth credential is
# still enforced inside the Next.js app (ELO-17 fail-closed) — Caddy only adds
# the TLS layer that the raw EC2 box lacks, so the Basic-Auth header is never
# sent in clear text. Without this file the dashboard stays loopback-only.
{
	email {{EMAIL}}
}

{{DOMAIN}} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3100
}
